es", "History of gonococcal urethritis and unprotected sexual activity"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute appendicitis: Atypical for right upper quadrant localization", "Gastrointestinal bleeding: No melena or hematochezia reported", "Alcoholic hepatitis: Chronic pattern more consistent with her alcohol use history", "Pelvic inflammatory disease: Less likely given right upper quadrant focus"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension with tachycardia (suggestive of shock or sepsis)", "Fever (37.5°C) indicating possible infection", "Unprotected sexual activity + positive pregnancy test pending"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Gynecologic Emergency with Right Upper Quadrant Presentation", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5427466432324973, "posterior": 0.5952329152168784, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The systemic compromise could theoretically occur in acute pancreatitis, but absence of epigastric/back pain makes this less likely."], "evidence_against": ["RUQ pain is atypical for gynecologic emergencies, but β-hCG testing remains warranted to exclude pregnancy-related causes."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Hepatic Vascular Emergency", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.083, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The absence of liver enzyme elevation or coagulopathy reduces the likelihood of Budd-Chiari syndrome, though other hepatic vascular emergencies might not requi…"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Biliary Obstruction with Systemic Symptoms", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.001, "danger": 0.85, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_