demia as the pancreatitis mechanism?", "summary": "Without laboratory confirmation of hypertriglyceridemia or elevated pancreatic enzymes, this mechanism cannot be sustained as the primary diagnosis."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the absence of IgG4-related findings (e.g., lymphadenopathy, dacryoadenitis) in the physical exam inconsistent with autoimmune pancreatitis as the primary diagnosis?", "summary": "The absence of IgG4-related systemic features makes autoimmune pancreatitis an unlikely explanation for the RUQ pain and systemic compromise."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the lack of documented abnormal liver enzymes or coagulopathy in the evidence inconsistent with a hepatic vascular emergency?", "summary": "The absence of liver enzyme elevation or coagulopathy reduces the likelihood of Budd-Chiari syndrome, though other hepatic vascular emergencies might not require these findings."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the combination of sudden pain exacerbation during exercise and systemic hemodynamic instability (hypotension, tachycardia) strongly support ovarian torsion as the cause of referred right upper …", "summary": "Sudden pain during physical activity and systemic instability (hypotension, tachycardia) are consistent with ovarian torsion, though RUQ localization alone is atypical. This provides moderate support for the diagnosis."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is the absence of adnexal tenderness on physical exam inconsistent with ovarian torsion as the cause of systemic compromise and right upper quadrant pain?", "summary": "Lack of adnexal tenderness weakens ovarian torsion as the primary diagnosis but does not exclude it due to the possibility of referred pain without pelvic findings. This provides minor reduction in likelihood."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.459], ["B1.3", 0.372], ["B4", 0.112]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.543], ["B1.3", 0.514], ["B2", 0.14]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.595], ["B1.3", 0.578], ["B2", 0.083]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Hypotension (80/40 mmHg) with tachycardia (110 bpm) indicates shock. Pending β-hCG testing necessitates urgent exclusion of life-threatening pregnancy-related causes (ectopic pregnancy/hemoperitoneum) and other acute intra-abdominal emergencies.", "required_actions": ["Continue aggressive IV fluid resuscitation", "Prepare for emergent ultrasound or surgical consultation if β-hCG is positive", "Monitor for response to fluids and escalate to blood transfusion/collaborative care if hemodynamic instability persists"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "[static mode override] Emergency override is active due to hypotension (80/40 mmHg) with tachycardia (110 bpm) indicating shock. Pending β-hCG results require immediate preparation for emergent ultrasound/surgical consultation if positive, and further expansion would delay critical intervention. — emergency_override suppressed in static_diagnosis_qa mode"}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.65, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.5782310064092846, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely the diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Ectopic implantation of a blastocyst"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Inflammation of the pancreas"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Obstruction of blood flow through the hepatic vein"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Obstruction of the common bile duct by radio-opaque stones"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Vascular ectasia within the liver"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Adnexal tenderness', 'epigastric pain', 'gas', 'pain', 'acute pancreatitis', 'back pain', 'Abnormal liver physiology'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_kn